Modifications by TechnoWolfTV (2025-2026)

The following changes were made to the original weather_pack mod by
Artūras Norkus (xeranas) and are released under the same MIT License above.

-- Administrative / housekeeping --

- Removed deprecated files: depends.txt, description.txt
- mod.conf: Updated to modern format (name, description, optional_depends).

-- Weather frequency rebalancing --

All weather types reduced to approximately 25% of their original spawn
frequency to better suit long-play sessions:

- light_rain:  0.0375  (was 0.15)
- rain:        0.025   (was 0.1)
- heavy_rain:  0.015   (was 0.06, tropical: 0.1)
- snow:        0.05    (was 0.2)
- snowstorm:   0.0125  (was 0.05)
- thunder:     0.8     (restored to original — controls how quickly thunder
                        kicks in once heavy_rain is active, not spawn rate)

-- Shelter-aware sound attenuation --

- utils.lua: Added shelter detection (get_shelter_factor), per-weather gain
  profiles (outdoor/indoor/cave), and sound fading via minetest.sound_fade.

- weathers/light_rain.lua, rain.lua, heavy_rain.lua, snowstorm.lua,
  thunder.lua: Integrated shelter-aware sound attenuation throughout.

-- New weather types --

- weathers/light_fog.lua, moderate_fog.lua, dense_fog.lua: Three fog
  densities implemented via Luanti's set_sky fog table API (not particles),
  giving true engine-level atmospheric depth. Each tier applies a sky tint,
  cloud color/density overlay, 25% lighting reduction (day/night ratio 0.75),
  and engine fog at progressive distances (100/50/20 nodes). Both fog
  distance and lighting fade in over 10 seconds on entry and out over 10
  seconds on exit. Fog is suppressed entirely when the player is indoors
  (checked via get_shelter_factor, throttled to once per second). Biome-aware
  (no fog in dry biomes). Fog does not appear during heavy_rain or snowstorm.
  moderate_fog displaces light_fog; dense_fog displaces both lighter tiers.
  On natural end, dense_fog usually lifts to moderate_fog; moderate_fog
  sometimes lifts to light_fog.

- weathers/pds_severe_thunderstorm.lua: Five-phase "Particularly Dangerous
  Situation" severe thunderstorm with progressive sky darkening, ominous
  green sky hue, rain buildup, day/night ratio override, low rumble sound
  during onslaught, escalating lightning, and proportional wind-down.
  Rare tier (chance 0.0075).

- weathers/severe_thunderstorm.lua: Five-phase severe thunderstorm, less
  intense counterpart to PDS: no green sky, no rumble, reduced darkness,
  reduced lightning frequency, shorter phase durations. More common tier
  (chance 0.015).

-- Modifications to existing weather types --

- weathers/overcast.lua: New weather type applying heavy_rain's sky and
  cloud colors with no rain, sound, or lighting changes. Sky-only overcast
  effect. Frequency matches rain (chance 0.025, check_interval 300s).

- weathers/clear.lua: New weather type that disables clouds and lets
  Luanti's default blue sky render unmodified. No sky layer, no particles,
  no sound, no lighting changes. Frequency matches overcast.

- weathers/heavy_rain.lua: Sky, sound, and rain particles all fade in over
  10 seconds on entry and out over 10 seconds on exit instead of switching
  instantly. Minimum active duration enforced before any end request is
  honored. Severe storms still override heavy_rain instantly. Admin
  stop/disable bypasses the taper and takes effect immediately.

- weathers/snowstorm.lua: Added a natural random end condition. The original
  had none — once started, it ran until manually stopped.

- weathers/severe_thunderstorm.lua, pds_severe_thunderstorm.lua: Fixed a
  multiplayer bug where a new player joining a running storm reset the phase
  machine back to Phase 1. Rain particles now visible through windows from
  indoors (removed an extra player-shelter gate that blocked all spawning).

-- Bug fixes and improvements --

- utils.lua: Added hw_utils.random_float() and corrected invalid non-integer
  math.random() calls in snow.lua, snowstorm.lua, and light_rain.lua.

- lib_happy_weather_api.lua: Added disconnect cleanup hook (stale per-player
  state was left behind when a player disconnected mid-weather). Added
  happy_weather.force_end() for instant admin stops. Added
  happy_weather.get_active_duration() to power elapsed-time display in
  /weather_status. Activated-at timestamp now cleared on weather end.

- abm.lua: Fire extinguishing covers both fire:basic_flame and
  lightning:dying_flame (the node the lightning mod creates on a strike).
  heavy_rain and both severe storm tiers extinguish outdoor fire quickly
  (~5 seconds average). rain extinguishes more slowly (~10 seconds average).
  light_rain never extinguishes fire.

-- Command additions --

- commands.lua: Added /disable_weather and /enable_weather (persists across
  restarts). Added /stop_weather all. Added /weather_status (shows active
  with elapsed time, enabled, and disabled). Admin stop and disable now use
  force_end for instant effect on all weather types.

-- New assets --

- sounds/severe-storm-rumble.ogg: Used during pds_severe_thunderstorm
  onslaught only. "Low Rumbling" by Musheran (opengameart.org).
  License: CC BY (creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/)
